Package: huncMarkovNCD
Type: Package
Title: Zelravine Versus Usual Care for Nocturnal Cortical Dysrhythmia: A Markov Cost-Effectiveness Model
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ian", "Cromwell", email = "healthyuncertainty@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A cohort Markov state-transition cost-effectiveness model of zelravine versus usual care for Nocturnal Cortical Dysrhythmia (NCD), with a one-year decision-tree phase, one-time re-treatment states, deterministic and probabilistic (PSA) analysis, cost-effectiveness plane, acceptability curve, and an interactive Shiny interface. The disease, therapy, sponsor, trial data and all inputs are fictional and were invented for methods illustration; only the background mortality table (CDC WONDER, 2020) is real public data. The manufacturer's base case report is included in the package.
